### Stock Service - example requests (IntelliJ HTTP Client)
### Start: docker compose (MySQL) -> eureka-server -> stock-service
### Direct calls on port 8082. Sample stock uses the same SKUs as product-service.
### Run the REQUESTS IN ORDER within each section - later requests depend on earlier ones.

@baseUrl = http://localhost:8082
@stock = {{baseUrl}}/api/v1/stock
@reservations = {{stock}}/reservations

### 1. Health - expect "status":"UP" with "db" (MySQL) UP
GET {{baseUrl}}/actuator/health

### ===================== AVAILABILITY (product selected) =====================

### 2. In stock - expect "available": true, "status": "IN_STOCK" (MacBook Air, 25 on hand)
GET {{stock}}/LAP-APL-001/availability?quantity=2

### 3. Out of stock - expect "available": false, "status": "OUT_OF_STOCK" (MacBook Pro)
GET {{stock}}/LAP-APL-002/availability

### 4. Low stock, asking for more than exists - expect "available": false, "availableQuantity": 2
GET {{stock}}/LAP-HP-002/availability?quantity=5

### 5. Lower-case SKU works too (SKUs are case-insensitive)
GET {{stock}}/lap-apl-001/availability

### 6. Unknown SKU - expect 404 "Stock item not found"
GET {{stock}}/NOPE-000/availability

### 7. Whole cart in one call - expect "allAvailable": false,
#    because PHN-ONE-001 is out of stock and XYZ-999 is NOT_STOCKED.
#    The two LAP-APL-001 lines are merged into one line with quantity 3.
POST {{stock}}/availability
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "items": [
    { "sku": "LAP-APL-001", "quantity": 1 },
    { "sku": "AUD-APL-001", "quantity": 2 },
    { "sku": "PHN-ONE-001", "quantity": 1 },
    { "sku": "XYZ-999", "quantity": 1 },
    { "sku": "LAP-APL-001", "quantity": 2 }
  ]
}

### ===================== RESERVATION FLOW (product ordered) =====================
### In production only the order-service calls these (the gateway blocks them).

### 8. Reserve for order ORD-1001 - expect 201 Created, "status": "RESERVED"
POST {{reservations}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-1001",
  "items": [
    { "sku": "LAP-APL-001", "quantity": 2 },
    { "sku": "AUD-APL-001", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### 9. Stock after reserving - expect quantityOnHand 25, quantityReserved 2, quantityAvailable 23
GET {{stock}}/LAP-APL-001

### 10. SAME request again (e.g. order-service retry after a timeout)
#     Expect 200 OK (not 201) and the SAME reservation - nothing reserved twice.
POST {{reservations}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-1001",
  "items": [
    { "sku": "LAP-APL-001", "quantity": 2 },
    { "sku": "AUD-APL-001", "quantity": 1 }
  ]
}

### 11. Get the reservation
GET {{reservations}}/ORD-1001

### 12. Confirm (order completed) - expect "status": "CONFIRMED"
POST {{reservations}}/ORD-1001/confirm

### 13. Stock after confirming - expect quantityOnHand 23, quantityReserved 0, quantityAvailable 23
GET {{stock}}/LAP-APL-001

### 14. Release a confirmed reservation - expect 409 "Operation not allowed"
POST {{reservations}}/ORD-1001/release

### ----- cancellation flow -----

### 15. Reserve for order ORD-1002
POST {{reservations}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-1002",
  "items": [ { "sku": "TAB-APL-001", "quantity": 3 } ]
}

### 16. Release (order cancelled) - expect "status": "RELEASED"; TAB-APL-001 is fully available again
POST {{reservations}}/ORD-1002/release

### 17. Confirm a released reservation - expect 409
POST {{reservations}}/ORD-1002/confirm

### ----- not enough stock -----

### 18. All-or-nothing - expect 409 "Insufficient stock" with a "shortages" list for LAP-HP-002.
#     AUD-SNY-001 IS available, but is NOT reserved either, because the order can't be fulfilled.
POST {{reservations}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "ORD-1003",
  "items": [
    { "sku": "AUD-SNY-001", "quantity": 1 },
    { "sku": "LAP-HP-002", "quantity": 5 }
  ]
}

### 19. Check that AUD-SNY-001 was NOT reserved - expect quantityReserved 0
GET {{stock}}/AUD-SNY-001

### 20. Unknown order - expect 404 "Reservation not found"
GET {{reservations}}/ORD-9999

### ===================== STOCK MANAGEMENT =====================

### 21. List all stock, page 0 (sorted by SKU)
GET {{stock}}?page=0&size=10

### 22. What needs restocking? - expect 9 items (low stock + out of stock)
GET {{stock}}?lowStockOnly=true

### 23. Delivery received: +20 MacBook Pro - status changes from OUT_OF_STOCK to IN_STOCK
POST {{stock}}/LAP-APL-002/adjustments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantityChange": 20,
  "reason": "Delivery from supplier, delivery note DN-5521"
}

### 24. Write off more than exists - expect 409 (on-hand can't go below 0 or below reserved)
POST {{stock}}/LAP-HP-002/adjustments
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantityChange": -10,
  "reason": "Damaged in warehouse"
}

### 25. Stock count correction (absolute values)
PUT {{stock}}/MON-SAM-001
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "quantityOnHand": 14,
  "reorderLevel": 4
}

### 26. Create stock for a new product - expect 201 + Location header
POST {{stock}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "LAP-FRM-001",
  "quantityOnHand": 10,
  "reorderLevel": 2
}

### 27. Same SKU again - expect 409 "Duplicate stock item"
POST {{stock}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "lap-frm-001",
  "quantityOnHand": 5,
  "reorderLevel": 1
}

### 28. Delete it - expect 204
DELETE {{stock}}/LAP-FRM-001

### 29. Delete a SKU used by orders - expect 409 (LAP-APL-001 has reservation history)
DELETE {{stock}}/LAP-APL-001

### ===================== VALIDATION =====================

### 30. Invalid body - expect 400 with "errors" for sku, quantityOnHand and reorderLevel
POST {{stock}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "sku": "bad sku!",
  "quantityOnHand": -1
}

### 31. Invalid query parameter - expect 400, "errors": {"quantity": "quantity must be at least 1"}
GET {{stock}}/LAP-APL-001/availability?quantity=0

### 32. Invalid reservation - expect 400 for orderId and items
POST {{reservations}}
Content-Type: application/json

{
  "orderId": "",
  "items": []
}
